# A link to a tailnet name failing while this computer is off its tailnet, the owner's plan of
# 2026-10-14: "A status-line reason when a tailnet address fails and this computer isn't on a
# tailnet". TCP to my-pi.tail1234.ts.net, which no resolver here knows, with Tailscale signed out
# (tests/gui/fake-tailscale.sh's needslogin): the status line says why, once.
#
# Needs no link: tools/gui-headless.sh tailscale-reason
screen fly
window 1600x1200
budget 15
env XDG_DATA_HOME $WORK
env MP_CONFIG_XML $WORK/config.xml
env FAKE_TAILSCALE_STATE needslogin

within 12
expect tailscale.state signed-out
click main-port
expect link.ports >= 5
# The list's thirty rows end before TCP on a computer with many serial ports.
reveal main-port-list main-port-TCP
click main-port-TCP
expect link.port TCP
click main-connect
expect link.prompt remote host
key ctrl+u
type my-pi.tail1234.ts.net
key Return
expect link.prompt remote Port
key ctrl+u
type 5760
key Return
within 20
expect status ~ my-pi.tail1234.ts.net is a Tailscale name, and this computer is not on a tailnet (Tailscale: signed out)
